I have thoroughly explored the codebase. Here is the complete report.

---

# Report: "Next exercise / task" navigation and visual cue flow in learn-p5

## 0. Hierarchy clarification (important — the terminology is mixed in the code)

Defined in `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/data/types.ts` (lines 16–42):

```
Course (data file = a "module" in user-facing copy)
  └─ Exercise  (a "lesson" in many code paths; route param = `[id]`)
       └─ ExerciseTask  (a "task"; an exercise may have 0+ tasks)
```

- `Course.slug` → user-facing "module" (`Course.moduleName`).
- `Exercise.id` → router param `id`, route `/learn/[course]/[id]`.
- `Exercise.tasks?: ExerciseTask[]` → optional multi-step tasks within one exercise.

So the user's phrasing "complete all tasks/exercises then go to next exercise" maps to:

- Inside one Exercise with `tasks[]`: completing all **tasks** advances to the next **exercise**.
- Between Exercises: route navigation inside the same Course (the "module").

There is **no separate "module" navigation step** between exercises — the "module" is just the Course wrapper. Course-to-course navigation is done by the user via the `/learn` list and the `ExerciseCard`.

---

## 1. Visual cue shown when an exercise finishes (the "Next →" cue)

### The cue is the `Toast` component
- File: `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/Toast.tsx` (full file, 142 lines)
- Triggered from: `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` lines **723–763** (the `useEffect` keyed on `state.completed`):

```tsx
// line 728
showToast("✓ Exercise completed!", "Next →", handleToastNext, "success");
```

- The icon is `check-circle` (success tone) — see `showToast` definition at lines **158–167** and the `Toast` prop `icon=…` at lines **1046–1049** of `[id].tsx`.
- The "Next →" string is the `actionLabel` of `Toast`. Tapping it calls `toastActionRef.current`, which is `handleToastNext`.
- The toast auto-dismisses after 4000 ms (`Toast.tsx` line 26 default) and slides up via `Animated.timing` (lines 48–53). If the user does nothing, the toast disappears and **no navigation happens** (see section 2).

### Rendering on screen
`Toast.tsx` is an absolutely-positioned `Animated.View` pinned to the top of the screen (lines 103–119):
- Spring-in: `Animated.spring(translateY, { toValue: 0, tension: 80, friction: 10 })` (lines 40–45).
- Slide-out: `Animated.timing(translateY, { toValue: -120, duration: 200 })` (lines 48–53).
- Layout: a row with a `MaterialCommunityIcons` glyph (`check-circle`/`alert-circle`, lines 86–87) + the message, and (optional) the action button on the right (lines 92–98).
- Color tone: success = `colors.success`, failure = `colors.error` (lines 35–36).

Inside the exercise screen it is mounted at `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` lines **1040–1050**.

> Note: this same `Toast` is reused for many things (task-complete interim message, "Task N/M complete", error messages, theme update notice), so it is the **only** completion-cue mechanism. It is a generic top-of-screen banner, not a dedicated celebratory "next exercise" overlay.

---

## 2. "All exercises complete" logic and whether navigation is automatic

### Task-level completion (inside a single exercise)
- Validation runs in the in-WebView bridge script, `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts`:
  - Lines **1180–1189** (no-pixel rules path): if there are tasks and `ACTIVE_TASK_INDEX < TASKS.length - 1`, it posts `taskComplete`; otherwise `exerciseComplete`.
  - Lines **1198–1206** (`postSuccess`, pixel-rule path): same logic.
- Received in React Native at `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` lines **460–477**:

```tsx
case "exerciseComplete":
  dispatch({ type: "RUN_DONE" });
  dispatch({ type: "EXERCISE_COMPLETE" });
  break;
case "taskComplete": {
  dispatch({ type: "RUN_DONE" });
  const totalTasks = state.exercise?.tasks?.length ?? 0;
  const hasMore = state.exercise?.tasks && msg.taskIndex < totalTasks - 1;
  if (hasMore && totalTasks > 1) {
    setTimeout(() => {
      showToast(`Task ${msg.taskIndex + 1}/${totalTasks} complete`, undefined, undefined, "success");
    }, 480);  // waits for in-WebView fade-through (~450ms)
  }
  dispatch({ type: "TASK_COMPLETE", taskIndex: msg.taskIndex });
  break;
}
```

- Reducer logic (`exerciseReducer`, lines **96–105**):
```tsx
case "TASK_COMPLETE": {
  const completedTasks = [...state.completedTasks, action.taskIndex];
  const hasMoreTasks = state.exercise?.tasks && action.taskIndex < state.exercise.tasks.length - 1;
  return {
    ...state,
    completedTasks,
    currentTaskIndex: hasMoreTasks ? action.taskIndex + 1 : state.currentTaskIndex,
    completed: !hasMoreTasks,   // ← all tasks done => exercise completed
  };
}
```

So: `state.completed` becomes `true` when the last task finishes (or immediately on `EXERCISE_COMPLETE` for exercises with no `tasks[]`).

### The completion side-effect (and next-exercise navigation)
`/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` lines **723–763**:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!state.completed || !state.exercise) return;
  const ex = state.exercise;
  const key = `${course}/${ex.id}`;
  showToast("✓ Exercise completed!", "Next →", handleToastNext, "success");

  (async () => {
    const durationMs = runStartTimeRef.current ? Date.now() - runStartTimeRef.current : undefined;
    const newlyUnlocked = await recordCompletion(`${course}/${ex.id}`, durationMs);
    if (newlyUnlocked.length > 0) {
      const first = ACHIEVEMENTS.find((a) => a.id === newlyUnlocked[0]);
      if (first) {
        // Defer slightly so the exercise-completion toast doesn't overlap.
        setTimeout(() => showToast(`🏆 ${first.title} unlocked`, undefined, undefined, "success"), 2200);
      }
    }
    const val = await AsyncStorage.getItem("completedLessons");
    const arr: string[] = val ? JSON.parse(val) : [];
    if (!arr.includes(key)) {
      arr.push(key);
      await AsyncStorage.setItem("completedLessons", JSON.stringify(arr));
    }
    const courseData = await loadCourse(course);
    if (!courseData) return;
    const allDone = courseData.exercises.every((l) => arr.includes(`${course}/${l.id}`));  // ← "all exercises complete"
    if (allDone) {
      const prev = await AsyncStorage.getItem("completedCourses");
      const courses: string[] = prev ? JSON.parse(prev) : [];
      if (!courses.includes(course)) {
        courses.push(course);
        await AsyncStorage.setItem("completedCourses", JSON.stringify(courses));
      }
    }
  })();
}, [state.completed, state.exercise, course, webViewReady, handleToastNext, showToast]);
```

Key findings:

- The "all exercises complete" check is **only** `courseData.exercises.every(l => arr.includes(...))` at lines **751–753**. Its only side-effect is to add the course slug to `completedCourses` in AsyncStorage. **It does NOT trigger navigation, nor a celebratory end-of-course cue.**
- When the *individual* exercise becomes `completed` it calls `showToast("✓ Exercise completed!", "Next →", handleToastNext, …)`. The "Next →" **is a manual tappable action**, not an auto-trigger.
- `handleToastNext` is defined at lines **708–721**:

```tsx
const handleToastNext = useCallback(() => {
  setToastVisible(false);
  if (!state.exercise) return;
  loadCourse(course).then((courseData) => {
    if (!courseData) return;
    const currentIndex = courseData.exercises.findIndex((l) => l.id === id);
    if (currentIndex >= 0 && currentIndex < courseData.exercises.length - 1) {
      const nextLesson = courseData.exercises[currentIndex + 1];
      router.replace(`/learn/${course}/${nextLesson.id}`);  // ← next exercise within same course
    } else {
      router.replace(`/learn/${course}`);                    // ← last exercise: back to course list
    }
  });
}, [state.exercise, course, id, router]);
```

So:
- **Navigation between exercises within a module (Course) is MANUAL**: the user must tap "Next →" on the toast. There is no auto-advance.
- If the user lets the 4 s toast expire, nothing happens — they remain on the just-completed exercise.
- The same `router.replace(/learn/${course}/${nextLesson.id})` path is also reachable from the in-WebView `goToNextLesson` message (`[id].tsx` lines 490–501), but **`goToNextLesson` is never posted by the bridge script** — `grep` shows no `goToNextLesson` emit in `exerciseHtml.ts`. That handler is currently dead code / future hook.
- Course completion (`allDone === true`) has **no visual cue at all** on the exercise screen — it silently writes to `completedCourses`. The only place this surfaces visually is the `/learn` list (`/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/index.tsx`) which renders a completed badge/asterisk on the course card.

### Interim task-complete cue (between tasks within one exercise)
- `showToast(\`Task ${i+1}/${totalTasks} complete\`, …)` at `[id].tsx` line 472. Same `Toast` component, no action button. Auto-dismisses in 4 s.
- The actual progression to the next task is automatic via the reducer (`currentTaskIndex` increments, line 102), and the WebView instruction panel does a Material-3 "fade-through" animation (`exerciseHtml.ts` lines 111–131 and 828–878). So **next-task navigation is automatic, but next-exercise navigation is manual**.

---

## 3. Navigation between exercises / modules

### Between exercises within a course (the user's main ask)
- Path: `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` `handleToastNext` (lines 708–721), via `router.replace(`/learn/${course}/${nextLesson.id}`)`.
- The list of "next exercises" is rendered on the course landing page `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/index.tsx`:
  - "Next exercise" hero with a big `START` button — lines 218–269.
  - "Up Next" list of upcoming lessons with lock icons and a "trophy" for the last one — lines 271–362.
  - Progress bar within the hero — lines 254–267.
- Locking logic: `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/isExerciseLocked.ts` — an exercise is locked unless all earlier exercises in the same course are completed (`completedLessons` AsyncStorage list).

### Between modules (courses)
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/index.tsx` renders the list of courses via `<ExerciseCard>` (`/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/ExerciseCard.tsx`).
- `ExerciseCard` has a `Continue` button (lines 70–72, only when `isCurrent && onContinue`) and shows `check-circle` if `completed`, a `lock` if `locked`. There is **no animation between course cards** — they are flat `Pressable` rows.

So the navigation is:
```
/learn  →  /learn/[course]  →  /learn/[course]/[id]
   ↑                              ↑ manual "Next →" tap on Toast
   └── back-to-course on last exercise (router.replace)
```

`router.replace` is used everywhere (not `push`), so back-stack doesn't pile up.

---

## 4. Existing animation / visual-cue components you can reuse for a "more noticeable" cue

### What is already installed
- **`react-native-reanimated` 4.2.1** (in `package.json` line 46, plus `react-native-worklets` 0.7.4 line 52) — fully wired into the app.
- **`react-native-svg` 15.15.3** (line 49) — used in `ExerciseCard.tsx` for the asterisk glyph.
- **`expo-haptics`** (`package.json` line 35) — already used for the long-press cue at `[id].tsx` line 588 (`Haptics.impactAsync`).
- **No Lottie** dependency. (`grep` for `lottie` returns nothing in `src/`; not in `package.json`.)
- React Native built-in `Animated` is used in several places.

### Existing animated cue components available for reuse

| Component | File | Animation | Reusability for "noticeable next" cue |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Toast` | `src/components/Toast.tsx` | Top spring-in / slide-out via RN `Animated` (lines 31, 40–70); 4 s auto-dismiss; supports `actionLabel` + `tone` + custom icon | This is the *current* cue. Easy to extend (bigger text / longer duration / animated icon) but it is intentionally subtle. |
| `StreakToast` | `src/components/StreakToast.tsx` | RN `Animated` parallel spring + timing, plus a count-up number animation and an animated progress bar (lines 45–130) | Closest existing "celebratory" overlay — already includes a trophy/fire icon, milestone copy, and a progress bar. Good template for a "course complete" or "go to next module" celebratory cue. |
| `AchievementBadgeModal` | `src/components/AchievementBadgeModal.tsx` | Modal with `animationType="fade"`, horizontal paging `FlatList` of badges, dot pagination (lines 64–141). Static (no spring), but a full-screen celebratory modal | Best candidate to model a "course complete / next module" celebratory screen. Could be repurposed for end-of-course cue. |
| `ShakeModal` | `src/components/ShakeModal.tsx` | RN `Animated` parallel spring + opacity (lines 35–63) | Reusable modal action-sheet pattern with haptics-friendly per-action variants. |
| `SplashScreen` | `src/components/SplashScreen.tsx` | `react-native-reanimated` `useAnimatedStyle` + `withTiming` (lines 3–10, 68–89) | Reference for Reanimated-based entrances. |
| `SideDrawer` | `src/components/SideDrawer.tsx` | Reanimated `useAnimatedStyle` for backdrop + drawer slide (lines 3–8, 27–85) | Reference pattern if you want a slide-up "next exercise" panel. |
| Onboarding `[slide].tsx` | `src/app/onboarding/[slide].tsx` | Reanimated (lines 6–10, 72, 354) | Reusable full-screen Reanimated overlay pattern. |
| In-WebView "fade-through" | `exerciseHtml.ts` lines 111–131, 828–878 | CSS keyframes `task-fade-through-out`/`-in` (Material 3) | Used only for task→task transitions inside the WebView; not the React layer. |
| In-WebView tutorial overlay | `exerciseHtml.ts` lines 303–366 (CSS) and 1445–1519 (JS) | `"tut-overlay"` with dim backdrop, cutout highlight box, arrow-pointed card; gated by `exerciseNumber === 1` and dismissed via `localStorage` | Only shown on exercise 1; React-side equivalent doesn't exist, but the SVG/HTML pattern is reusable as a template. |

### `expo-haptics` availability
- Imported in `[id].tsx` line 6 (`expo-haptics`), invoked at line 588 for long-press feedback. A "more noticeable" completion cue could easily add `Haptics.notificationAsync(Haptics.NotificationFeedbackType.Success)` on `state.completed`.

---

## Summary of the flow (one-liner)

1. User presses Run → in-WebView validation runs (`exerciseHtml.ts` lines ~1180–1206) → posts `taskComplete` or `exerciseComplete`.
2. `[id].tsx` `handleMessage` (lines 460–477) reduces `TASK_COMPLETE`/`EXERCISE_COMPLETE`. For intermediate tasks it shows a `Toast` "Task i/N complete" (line 472) after a 480 ms delay timed to the WebView fade-through.
3. When the last task (or the no-task exercise) completes, `state.completed` flips true → the effect at lines 723–763 fires, calling `showToast("✓ Exercise completed!", "Next →", handleToastNext, "success")`.
4. The `Toast` (`src/components/Toast.tsx`) springs in from the top, shows `check-circle` + "Next →" button, auto-dismisses in 4 s. **Navigation to the next exercise is manual** — tapping "Next →" calls `handleToastNext` (lines 708–721) which does `router.replace('/learn/<course>/<nextId>')`; if it was the last exercise, it routes back to `/learn/<course>`.
5. After completing the last exercise, there is *no* distinct course-completion cue — only a silent write to `completedCourses` AsyncStorage; the only visual reward is a deferred `Toast` for newly-unlocked achievements (line 737) and the existing `AchievementBadgeModal` invoked from elsewhere (dashboard).

The current cue is **a single top-of-screen banner** (`Toast`) that lasts 4 s and requires a tap on a small "Next →" link to advance. Nothing flashes, pulses, scales, or plays a celebration on completion — and there is no automatic advance. All the infrastructure for a more noticeable cue (Reanimated, Haptics, Lottie-free but full-screen modals already built) is in place, but unused for this moment.

### Key file paths
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` — exercise screen + completion logic (lines 94–109 reducer, 460–506 message handler, 708–721 handleToastNext, 723–763 completion effect, 1040–1050 Toast render).
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/Toast.tsx` — the actual cue UI.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts` — WebView validation that emits `taskComplete`/`exerciseComplete` (lines 1180–1206) and the per-task fade-through animation (lines 111–131, 828–878).
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/index.tsx` — the "Next exercise" hero and "Up Next" list (lines 218–362).
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/isExerciseLocked.ts` — sequential lock logic.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/data/types.ts` — `Course → Exercise → ExerciseTask` hierarchy.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/StreakToast.tsx` and `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/AchievementBadgeModal.tsx` — existing celebratory animated components reusable for a "more noticeable" cue.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/hooks/useAchievements.ts` — `recordCompletion` (line 69) used in the completion effect.
- `/workspaces/learn-p5/package.json` lines 35–52 — available animation libraries (`react-native-reanimated@4.2.1`, `react-native-worklets@0.7.4`, `expo-haptics@~55.0.9`, `react-native-svg@15.15.3`). **No Lottie.**
